  "packageLinking": "The base DFS is each project's Design Fee sheet: its headings (\"GFC | Tower—01\", \"GFC | Individual Homes\", \"GFC | Independent Subgrade Structure—Block 04\" …) are the WBS tree above packages, nested by the sheet's outline numbers, and every coded row is a package under the heading it sits beneath. The stage prefix \"GFC | \" is dropped from node names (the source label is kept). A drawing's package: (1) its batch code is the package code with an optional discipline prefix and an unpadded number (AR-T01-1 → T01-01, ST-TXV-12 → TXV-12, BB01-2 → BB01-2); (2) only when the batch names no DFS package, the drawing-list heading it sits under, if that heading names exactly one package by code or location token (\"Individual Home V40\" → V40-01), logged as BATCH_RESOLVED_BY_DFS_HEADING. A batch marked \"-NA\", a heading naming several packages, or no match leaves the drawing unmapped (BATCH_WITHOUT_FEE_PACKAGE / DRAWING_PACKAGE_AMBIGUOUS) — nothing is guessed. Tower 09 has no current Design Fee sheet; the Commercial 03-Year Plan (2023) Design Fee sheet is its only package definition and is used as its base DFS. Tower 09 register batches <discipline>-ISS-n and <discipline>-MP-n carry no heading; the location (ISS, MP) is the initials of exactly one Design Fee group (Independent Subgrade Structure, Master Plan) and n is the package's position in that group — logged as BATCH_RESOLVED_BY_GROUP_ORDINAL.",
  "dfsHierarchy": {
    "labelPrefix": "^GFC\\s*\\|\\s*",
    "nodeTypes": [],
    "resolveUnlinkedByHeading": true
  },
